  data:  # c4f1
    kind: work_item  # c4f1
    title: "ADR-0023 §6 Phase 3 (protocol-call subset): migrate http_calls / grpc_calls / graphql_calls to calls + meta['protocol']"  # c4f1
    status: todo_soft  # c4f1
    priority: 3  # c4f1
    parent:  # c4f1
    tags:  # c4f1
    - concept_audit  # c4f1
    - protocol_linkers  # c4f1
    isbefore: []  # c4f1
    duplicate_of: []  # c4f1
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c4f1
    pr_ref:  # c4f1
    description: "Per the ADR-0023 §6 revision (this PR), migrate the protocol-call family — the natural-next Phase 3 subset after WI-mokam-jalig (dst-kind), WI-mifor-vabul (bridge), WI-vasik-jofiv (publish/dispatch), and WI-hahap-farid (IPC). Three endpoint_shape values fold to canonical 'calls' + meta['protocol']:\n\nVALUES TO MIGRATE:\n- http_calls → calls + meta['protocol']='http'  (producer: linkers/http.py)\n- grpc_calls → calls + meta['protocol']='grpc'  (producer: linkers/grpc.py)\n- graphql_calls → calls + meta['protocol']='graphql'  (producer: linkers/graphql.py)\n\nThis is a strict-pattern subset: same fold target shape across all three values, mirroring WI-mifor-vabul's bridge_kind closure. The fold target is already canonical (\"calls\" is in the registry); the migration is purely a producer-side rename plus a meta key.\n\nCONSUMER-SIDE WORK (in the same PR):\n- compact.CROSS_CUTTING_EDGE_TYPES currently contains http_calls — drop it (canonical 'calls' is already in the set, so cross-cutting endpoint seeding still picks up HTTP edges via the canonical name).\n- taint.TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES currently contains grpc_calls — drop it (canonical 'calls' is already in the set; gRPC taint propagation transfers automatically).\n- io_boundary._TRACEABLE_EDGE_TYPES currently contains grpc_calls — drop it (same reason).\n\nPROTOCOL META-KEY ENUMERATION:\nReuse the existing meta['protocol'] vocabulary (already populated by the IPC family migration WI-hahap-farid for protocol='ipc'). The closed enumeration (analogous to BRIDGE_KINDS) becomes {ipc, http, grpc, graphql} and gains a new constant PROTOCOL_KINDS in hypergumbo_core.edge_types per the ADR-0015 access_mode pattern.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n- All three endpoint_shape values have zero production emit sites (drift linter confirms via test_every_edge_type_named_set_is_a_subset_of_registry — the values stay in the registry as deprecated until Phase 4b' prunes them).\n- meta['protocol'] gets a closed enumeration constant PROTOCOL_KINDS = frozenset({'ipc', 'http', 'grpc', 'graphql'}) documented in hypergumbo_core.edge_types.\n- Consumer enumerations in compact, taint, io_boundary drop the deprecated values; per-package coverage stays at 100%.\n- Tag awaits_bakeoff_validation per AGENTS.md §Bakeoff Validation Discipline. A DEEP cohort with HTTP/gRPC/GraphQL targets confirms centrality / slice / sketch behavior holds. Suggested cohort: a FastAPI repo (HTTP), a grpc-server-go repo (gRPC), an apollo-server repo (GraphQL), or one polyglot repo per family that has heavy use.\n\nPHASE 4b' FOLLOW-UP (separate item, gated on this PR's bakeoff validation): once bakeoff clears, file a mini-Phase-4b' to prune http_calls / grpc_calls / graphql_calls from the registry + bump SCHEMA_VERSION 0.4.0 → 0.5.0 (or a patch bump per ADR-0014's protocol if these values were already x-deprecated at 0.4.0 — they were). After Phase 4b' lands, the strict-mode pre-commit flip (WI-mumok) becomes safe.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:\n- HARD: WI-mokam-jalig (Phase 3 parent — done) + WI-vomoj-suhaz (Phase 4b first ship — done). The migration pattern, the registry shape, and the consumer-side cleanup pattern are all established.\n- SOFT: ADR-0023 already at Accepted (the §6 revision in this PR adds protocol-call as a named subset; the principle hasn't changed)."  # c4f1
    fields: {}  # c4f1
